   $q$What is $\frac{1.8 \times 10^{-3}}{6 \times 10^{5}}$ written in scientific notation?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$3 \\times 10^{-8}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"did-not-adjust-exponent-after-normalizing"},{"text":"$3 \\times 10^{1}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-exponents-when-dividing"},{"text":"$3 \\times 10^{-7}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adjusted-exponent-wrong-direction"},{"text":"$3 \\times 10^{-9}$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$3 \times 10^{-9}$$q$, $q$Divide the coefficients and subtract the exponents: $1.8 \div 6 = 0.3$ and $-3 - 5 = -8$, giving $0.3 \times 10^{-8}$. Since $0.3 = 3 \times 10^{-1}$, the quotient is $3 \times 10^{-8 + (-1)} = 3 \times 10^{-9}$. The choice $3 \times 10^{-8}$ changes 0.3 to 3 without lowering the exponent.$q$, 'draft', null)
